<title>AUSTRIA: Deutsche controls 17.2% of AMS.</title>
<headline>Deutsche controls 17.2% of AMS.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Grenfell Asset Management Limited and its parent Deutsche Bank AG together hold a total of 17.2 percent in Austrian microchip maker Austria Mikro Systeme International, AMS announced on Thursday.</p>
<p>The MGAM group holds 13 percent of the voting capital of AMS, while the Deutsche Bank group holds 4.2 percent on behalf of various funds, AMS said in an announcement published in daily Wiener Zeitung. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12 253</p>
